learnings:
  - 'In weaving, the harness is the frame of heddles that lifts warp threads so the weft can pass: ''Paradigm Harness'' is already Warpline vocabulary.'
  - 'The harness is a deletion project before a build project: the kernel already exists three times in three languages.'
  - 'Warpline and the harness are each other''s missing half: Warpline''s denominator is empty because one human edits serially; only an armada produces contested verdicts. The harness is Warpline''s instrument; Warpline is the harness''s merge law.'
  - The landscape gap list equals deepseek-harness's explicit refusal list.
  - '''Model-visible <=> logged'' and Warpline''s ''transfer != admission'' are the same law at two layers.'
  - 'Odysseus''s teacher flywheel is Paradigm''s classroom with roles inverted: more supply, same gate.'
  - Claude Code is the shell (bash); Conductor/constellation/Platform/Studio are terminal emulators and window managers; flow/constellation/atelier/Conductor are distros.
